# Ledgerly

You are working in a fictional B2B billing product. Write like a precise billing-ops tool, not a growth startup.

## Never invent prices

The catalog is only:

- Starter — $49 (4900 cents)
- Growth — $99 (9900 cents)
- Scale — $249 (24900 cents)

Do not invent $79, $199, usage overage, ARR, or "enterprise" pricing. Read amounts from `lib/plans.ts` or the seed. Format with `formatUsd`.

The catalog governs **app code, UI copy, and this repo's README**. Files under `workshop/data/**` are Ledgerly's own Collections 4.2 release material (products Collections, Nudge, Pulse; competitors Slatebook, Harborbill): quote them verbatim, cite the path or ID, and never import their numbers into the app catalog. Do not hand-edit generated artifacts; apparent typos may be planted.

## Never use real companies or PII

Customers come from the seed only: the ten Fieldnote book accounts (Acme North, Riverstone Labs, Cobalt Goods, Brightwell Labs, Oakiron Supply, Fieldnote Press, Silverpine Outfitters, Maple & Ember Co, Tidewatch Logistics, Copperleaf Atelier) plus the fourteen Collections 4.2 corpus accounts defined in `workshop/data/canon.json` (Northstar Fabrication through Redwood Components). Emails use `.example`. Operator is Avery Quinn. Do not drop in a prospect's logo, a real customer, or a real person.

## Seams

- Do not silently fix `tests/dispute-credit.test.ts` / `lib/dispute-credit.ts`. Restore with `git checkout -- lib/dispute-credit.ts` if it was changed.
- Seeded dispute `dsp_1043` claims $400 against a $249 Scale invoice on purpose. Do not "correct" that seed amount or the Resolution panel's live recompute.
- Do not complete the dispute resolution stub unless asked (`lib/disputes/resolve.ts`, the resolve API route, the panel buttons).
- Tab / Cmd-K TODOs in collection notes and settings are intentional.
- Restyles of KPI cards go through `app/globals.css` tokens only — no new hex, `components/kpi-card.tsx` plus `app/page.tsx` at most. Never commit a restyle to `main`.
- Skills in `.cursor/skills/` help someone play the app. Do not add use-case-solver skills. Do not add talk-track / speaker-note skills here.
- The Ledgerly runtime must not import `workshop/**` as modules. The `/analysis` routes read `workshop/data` and `workshop/runs` from disk, read-only, at request time — that is the one sanctioned touchpoint.
- The corpus remap to the Ledgerly world is done and locked. Never reintroduce retired pre-remap company or product names anywhere in this tree.

## Voice

Calm, specific, short. Prefer "invoice" and "credit" over "synergy." UI copy should sound like Fieldnote, not "Welcome to your app."
